{"strongs": "H5641", "word": "סָתַר", "translit": "sa.tar", "root": "סתר", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "hide, conceal", "definition": "סָתַר verb hide, conceal (Late Hebrew id. , derived species; ᵑ7 סְתַר Pa`el, Ithpa`al, Syriac Pe`al Passive participle, chiefly Pa`el, Ithpa`al, id. ; Arabic veil, conceal, hide , Lane 1304 ; Ethiopic (rare) Di 354 ); — Niph`al Perfect 3 masculine singular נִסְתָּ֑ר Prov 27:12 + Prov 22:3 Qr ( Kt וַיִּסָּתֵר ); 2 masculine singular נִסְתַּ֫רְתָּ 1Sam 20:19 1 plural נִסְתָּ֑רְנוּ Isa 28:15 , etc.; Imperfect 3 masculine singular יִסָּתֵר Hos 13:14 +; 1 singular אֶסָּתֵר Gen 4:14 +; 3 masculine plural יִסָּֽתְרוּ Amos 9:3 1 plural נִסָּתֵר Gen 31:49 , etc.; Imperative masculine singular הִסָּתֵר Jer 36:19 Infinitive construct לְהִסָּ֫תֶר שָׁם Job 34:22 Participle נִסְתָּר Ps 19:7 plural נִסְתָּרִים Deut 7:20 feminine plural נִסְתָּרֹת Deut 29:28 , וֺת - Ps 19:13 — 1. hide oneself , with בְּ local, 1Sam 20:5 ; 1Sam 20:24 ; 1Kgs 17:3 ; Jer 23:24 , so (figurative) Isa 28:15 with שָׁם 1Sam 20:19 ; Job 34:22 absolute Jer 36:19 ; Prov 22:3 ; Prov 27:12 ; Prov 28:28 ; Ps 89:47 with מִפְּנֵי person Deut 7:20 ; Job 13:20 , with מִן person Ps 55:13 . 2. be hid, concealed , especially figurative of escaping God's notice, with מִפְּנֵי person Gen 4:14 ( J ), מִלִּפְנֵי Jer 16:17 , מִנֶּגֶד עֵינַי Amos 9:3 , מֵעֵינַי Isa 65:16 ; Hos 13:14 (subject נֹחַם , i.e. I will not repent, change my purpose of judgment), מִן Ps 38:10 ; Isa 40:27 from heat of sun Ps 19:7 (i.e. it penetrates everywhere); from birds Job 28:21 (of place of wisdom); reciprocal אִישׁ מֵרֵעֵהוּ ׳ נִסּ Gen 31:49 ( J ) when we are hidden each from the other (i.e. separated); absolute Num 5:13 ; Job 3:23 ( whose way is hid that is, from himself), Zeph 2:3 (i.e. escape ׳ י 's judgment); participle hidden, secret things , in general Deut 29:28 of sins Ps 19:13 . Pi`el Imperative feminine singular סַתְּרִי Isa 16:3 carefully hide (i.e. shelter ) the outcasts (Moab speaks to Zion). Pu`al Participle feminine singular אַהֲבָה מְסֻתָּ֑רֶת Prov 27:5 love carefully concealed . Hithpa`el Imperfect 3 feminine singular תִּסְתַּתָּ֑ר Isa 29:14 Participle מִסְתַּתֵּר 1Sam 23:19 + 3 t.; — hide oneself carefully , of David's taking refuge with ( עִם ) Ziphites 1Sam 23:19 = Ps 54:2 (title), in ( בְּ ) a hill 1Sam 26:1 ׳ אֵל מ Isa 45:15 a God that completely hides himself . Hiph`il Perfect 3 masculine singular הִסְתִּיר Ps 10:11 ; Ps 22:25 2 masculine singular הִסְתַּ֫רְתָּ Ps 30:8 ; Isa 64:6 etc.; Imperfect 3 masculine singular יַסְתִּיר 1Sam 20:2 , וַיַּסְתֵּר Exod 3:6 ; Job 3:10 , suffix יַסְתִּרֵ֫נִי Ps 27:5 , וַיַּסְתִּרֵם Jer 36:26 3 feminine singular suffix וַתַּסְתִּירֵ֫הוּ 2Chr 22:11 1 singular וָאַסְתִּר Ezek 39:23 ; Ezek 39:24 , etc.; Imperative masculine singular הַסְתֵּר Ps 51:11 Infinitive absolute הַסְתֵּר Deut 31:18 ; Isa 57:17 construct הַסְתֵּר Prov 25:2 (see Kö i. 213 and references ; yet compare infinitive absolute אָכֹל v Prov 25:27 ), לַסְתִּר Isa 29:15 ( Ges «GKC:53q»§ 53q ); Participle מַסְתִּיר Isa 8:17 — conceal, hide: 1. a person from ( מִפְּנֵי ) enemy 2Kgs 11:2 = 2Chr 22:11 subject ׳ י , with מִן Ps 64:3 , absolute Jer 36:26 hide anything from ( מִן ) one 1Sam 20:2 , a thing, in general, Prov 25:2 anything (from ׳ י ; מִן in || clause) Isa 29:15 in general = shelter a person Job 14:13 , with בְּ local (subject ׳ י ) Ps 17:8 ; Ps 27:5 ; Ps 31:21 (all metaphor); toil ( עָמָל ), מֵעֵינָ֑י Job 3:10 commands from, מִן person (subject ׳ י ) Ps 119:19 hide one as arrow in quiver Isa 49:2 . 2. especially hide the face: \\ \\ a. literally, of Moses Exod 3:6 ( E ), usually figurative: \\ \\ b. subject ׳ י with מִן i.e. be not observant of sin Ps 51:11 , absolute Ps 10:11 more often \\ \\ c. ׳ י hides his face from ( מִן person), i.e. withdraws his favour, Mic 3:4 ; Isa 8:17 ; Isa 54:8 ; Isa 64:6 ; Deut 31:17 ; Deut 32:20 ; Jer 33:5 ; Ezek 39:23 ; Ezek 39:24 ; Ezek 39:29 ; Ps 13:2 ; Ps 22:25 ; Ps 27:9 ; Ps 69:18 ; Ps 88:15 ; Ps 102:3 ; Ps 143:7 absolute Deut 31:18 ; Job 13:24 ; Job 34:29 ; Ps 30:8 compare Ps 104:29 ; Ps 44:25 פָּנִים omitted Isa 57:17 compare Isa 59:2 your sins have hidden (his) face from ( מִן ) you; of hiding one's face from ( מִן ) shame, i.e. avoiding it Isa 50:6 (of servant of ׳ י ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5723')\">BDB5723</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H5641')\">H5641</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5722')\">BDB5722</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5724')\">BDB5724</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>סָתַר</bdbheb> <b>verb</b> <highlightword>hide, conceal</highlightword> (Late Hebrew <highlight>id.</highlight>, derived species; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Tg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ7</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <bdbheb>סְתַר</bdbheb> Pa`el, Ithpa`al, Syriac <placeholder3674/> Pe`al Passive participle, chiefly Pa`el, Ithpa`al, <highlight>id.</highlight>; Arabic <placeholder3675/> <highlight>veil, conceal, hide</highlight>, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Lane')\">Lane<sup>1304</sup></lookup>; Ethiopic <placeholder3676/> (rare) <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Di')\">Di<sup>354</sup></lookup>); — <div class=\"point\"><b>Niph`al</b> <highlight>Perfect</highlight> 3 masculine singular <bdbheb>נִסְתָּ֑ר</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Prov 27:12\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"27\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"27\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(20,27,12)\">Prov 27:12</ref> + <ref ref=\"Prov 22:3\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(20,22,3)\">Prov 22:3</ref> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Qr')\"><reflink>Qr</reflink></lookup> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Kt')\"><reflink>Kt</reflink></lookup> <bdbheb>וַיִּסָּתֵר</bdbheb>); 2 masculine singular <bdbheb>נִסְתַּ֫רְתָּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Sam 20:19\" b=\"9\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(9,20,19)\">1Sam 20:19</ref> 1 plural <bdbheb>נִסְתָּ֑רְנוּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 28:15\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\